# Google (Calendar + Gmail) OAuth for the assistant — copy to google.env and fill in (google.env is gitignored).
# ONE Cloud "Desktop app" client serves ALL accounts; per-account refresh tokens live in the token store.
# Setup walkthrough: GOOGLE_SETUP.md
# Gotcha: no inline "# comment" after a value — the whole line after = is the value.

# From Google Cloud console → APIs & Services → Credentials → OAuth client ID (type: Desktop app). Required.
GOOGLE_CLIENT_ID=
GOOGLE_CLIENT_SECRET=

# Optional. Space-separated OAuth scopes. Leave blank to use the default set (calendar + gmail.modify +
# gmail.send + userinfo.email + openid). Narrow it here if you want the assistant to have less.
GOOGLE_SCOPES=

# Optional. Where per-account refresh tokens are stored. Defaults to seneschal/state/google_tokens.json
# (gitignored). Only change if you want the token store somewhere else.
GOOGLE_TOKEN_STORE=

# Optional. Fixed loopback port for the one-time consent flow. Blank/0 = pick a free port automatically.
# Set a fixed port only if your OAuth client restricts redirect URIs to a specific http://127.0.0.1:PORT.
GOOGLE_OAUTH_PORT=
